From b9b6f978fdd1830663aa4627684be0984c88ede0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritika Chopra <r.chopra@vyos.io>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:13:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] T9238: pptp: close call socket when Outgoing-Call-Reply
 cannot be sent (port from accel-ppp 350)

The PPPoX socket created for the call is only handed to conn->ppp.fd
after the reply has been posted, so returning early on a post_msg()
failure leaks the descriptor: disconnect() knows nothing about it and
establish_ppp() has not run yet. The establish_ppp() failure path just
below already closes it.

Authored-by: Denys Fedoryshchenko <denys.f@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit f49ed06b26b2b3ea3a97589be2e51ceb2a084243)
---
 accel-pppd/ctrl/pptp/pptp.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pptp/pptp.c b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pptp/pptp.c
index 96194e22..c7426b34 100644
--- a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pptp/pptp.c
+++ b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pptp/pptp.c
@@ -340,8 +340,10 @@ static int pptp_out_call_rqst(struct pptp_conn_t *conn)
 		return -1;
 	}
 
-	if (send_pptp_out_call_rply(conn, msg, src_addr.sa_addr.pptp.call_id, PPTP_CALL_RES_OK, 0))
+	if (send_pptp_out_call_rply(conn, msg, src_addr.sa_addr.pptp.call_id, PPTP_CALL_RES_OK, 0)) {
+		close(pptp_sock);
 		return -1;
+	}
 
 	conn->call_id = src_addr.sa_addr.pptp.call_id;
 	conn->peer_call_id = msg->call_id;
